            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Green"}> Michael Green
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hirosi+Ooguri"} Hirosi Ooguri
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Schwarz"} John Schwarz
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Nondecoupling Supergravity from the Superstring
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom+Banks"}> Tom Banks
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Why I don’t Believe N= 8 SUGRA is Finite
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "http://www.gravity.psu.edu/events/supergravity/program.shtml"} Workshop “Supergravity versus Superstring Theory in the Ultraviolet”
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Renata+Kallosh"}> Renata Kallosh
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    The Ultraviolet Finiteness of
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi N
                          %mo =
                          %mn 8
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N=8
                    Supergravity
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1009.1135"} arXiv:1009.1135
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacques+Distler"}> Jacques Distler
                ,
                %em
                  Decoupling
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi N
                        %mo =
                        %mn 8
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N = 8
                  supergravity
                (
                %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/~distler/blog/archives/001235.html"}> blog post
                )
          %p
            Discussion along the lines of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twistor+string+theory"} twistor string theory
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scattering+amplitudes"} scattering amplitudes
            encoded by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+maps"} rational maps
            from a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+curve"} complex curve
            two
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twistor+space"} twistor space
          %ul
            %li#CachazoSkinner12
              %p
                Freddy Cachazo,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Skinner"} David Skinner
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Gravity from Rational Curves
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1207.0741"} arXiv:1207.0741
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.110.161301"} arXiv:10.1103/PhysRevLett.110.161301
            %li#Adamo15
              %p
                Tim Adamo,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Gravity with a cosmological constant from rational curves
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1508.02554"} arXiv:1508.02554
          %h4#on_gravitino_phenomenology On gravitino phenomenology
          %p
            A proposal for super-heavy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravitinos"} gravitinos
            as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dark+matter"} dark matter
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D4+N%3D8+supergravity"} D=4 N=8 supergravity
            into
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E10"} E10
            = succeed "-invariant" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/U-duality"} U-duality
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
          %ul
            %li#MeissnerNicolai18a
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Krzysztof+A.+Meissner"}> Krzysztof A. Meissner
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermann+Nicolai"} Hermann Nicolai
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Standard Model Fermions and Infinite-Dimensional R-Symmetries
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1804.09606"} arXiv:1804.09606
            %li#MeissnerNicolai18b
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Krzysztof+A.+Meissner"}> Krzysztof A. Meissner
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermann+Nicolai"} Hermann Nicolai
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Planck Mass Charged Gravitino Dark Matter
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.01441"} arXiv:1809.01441
          %p following the proposal towards the end of
          %ul
            %li#GellMann83
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Murray+Gell-Mann"}> Murray Gell-Mann
                , introductory talk at
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shelter_Island_Conference"} Shelter Island II
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Gell-Mann_ShelterIslandII_1983.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %p
                in:
                = succeed "." do
                  %em Shelter Island II: Proceedings of the 1983 Shelter Island Conference on Quantum Field Theory and the Fundamental Problems of Physics
          %h3#ReferencesGauged Gauged 4d supergravity
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauged+supergravity"} gauged supergravity
            in 4d originates around (
            %a{:href => "#CremmerJulia79"} Cremmer-Julia 79
            (where the
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E7"} E7
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/U-duality"} U-duality
            group was first seen)
          %p
            Discussion of reduction from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            includes
          %ul
            %li
              L. Andrianopoli,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riccardo+D%27Auria"} Riccardo D'Auria
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  4-D gauged supergravity analysis of Type IIB vacua on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi K
                          %mn 3
                        %mo ×
                        %msup
                          %mi T
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %msub
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_3 \times T^2 / \mathbb{Z}_2
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0302174"} arXiv:hep-th/0302174
          %p
            Perturbative finiteness properties of gauged 4d supergravity from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo =
                  %mn 8
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N = 8
            ungauged 4d supergravity is discussed in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "#BCDJR11"} BCDJR 11, p. 24
          %blockquote
            %p
              Another question is whether
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo =
                    %mn 8
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N = 8
              supergravity might point the way to other, more realistic finite (or well behaved) theories of quantum gravity, having less supersymmetry and (perhaps) chiral fermions. One step in this direction could be to examine the multiloop behavior of theories that can be thought of as spontaneously broken gauged
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo =
                    %mn 8
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N = 8
              supergravity [73], which are known to have improved ultraviolet behavior at one loop [74].
          %p
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "#FerraraMarrani12"} Ferrara-Marrani 12, p. 12
          %blockquote
            %p
              Another interesting aspect [21] which should be implied by UV finiteness of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo =
                    %mn 8
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 6
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 5
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N = 8, 6, 5
              supergravity in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo =
                    %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D = 4
              dimensions is that their gauged versions should be possibly UV finite, as well. Roughly speaking, this is related to the fact that gauging may be regarded as a spontaneous soft breaking of an unbroken gauge symmetry, and UV properties should not be affected by such a spontaneous breaking, as it happens in the Standard Model of electro-weak interactions.
          %h3#lift_to_string_theory_and_mtheory Lift to string theory and M-theory
          %p
            Descent of 4d
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒩
                  %mo =
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N} = 2
            Sugra from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIA+string+theory"} type IIA string theory
            is reviewed for instance in
          %ul
            %li
              Thomas Wyder, section 1.3 of
              %em Split attractor flow trees and black hole entropy in type II string theory
              (
              %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/record/1397778/"}> spire
              )
          %p
            Discussion of lifts of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauged+supergravity"} gauged
            4d supergravity to
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            includes
          %ul
            %li
              Walter H. Baron,
              %em Uplifting Maximal Gauged Supergravities
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1512.05567"}> arXiv:1512.05567
              )
